    "A second breakthrough in FlashAttention-3 is the exploitation of Warpgroup Matrix Multiply-Accumulate, or WGMMA. On Hopper, groups of four contiguous warps—forming a warpgroup of one hundred and twenty-eight threads—can issue asynchronous tensor core matrix multiplications directly from shared memory. This eliminates the legacy requirement of loading tensor fragments from shared memory into thread registers before invoking matrix multiply instructions. FlashAttention-3 organizes its execution pipeline into a ping-pong buffer structure: while warpgroup A executes WGMMA instructions on the current tile residing in shared memory, TMA asynchronously streams the subsequent tile into an alternate shared memory buffer.",
